<title>FRANCE: French Jan consumption up 1.9 pct, Dec revised.</title>
<headline>French Jan consumption up 1.9 pct, Dec revised.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>					    Jan    Dec     Nov     Jan 96</p>
<p> Total				   57.95  56.89   57.66    59.65</p>
<p> Total change (pct v pvs month)   1.9   -1.3    -0.8	n/a</p>
<p> Retail sector			 39.59  37.93   38.88    39.24</p>
<p> Durables				16.42  16.63   16.88    18.67</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   11.77  10.98   11.16    11.50</p>
<p> Other				   29.76  29.28   29.61    29.48</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month on month unless stated)</p>
<p>					    Jan    Dec     Nov   Jan yr/yr</p>
<p> Total				     1.9   -1.3    -0.8     -2.9</p>
<p> Retail sector			   4.4   -2.4     1.8	0.9</p>
<p> Durables				 -1.2   -1.5    -4.3    -12.0</p>
<p>    of which cars		    -11.5    5.2   -18.1    -27.6</p>
<p>    household equip		    5.2   -5.3     5.6     -0.9</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		     7.1   -1.6     0.5	2.3</p>
<p> Other				     1.6   -1.1     0.9	0.9</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452  </p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said it revised its December consumer spending figure to a month-on-month fall of 1.3 percent from its initial 0.8 percent fall announced on January 23.</p>
</text>
